course: dictionary
lesson: 7047
title: Passive voice: the thing that gets done
level: primary-6
stars: 0
explain: In most sentences the doer comes first: «The cat chased the mouse.» The cat is doing the chasing, so the cat comes first. This is the active voice.
explain: Sometimes we put the thing that gets the action first: «The mouse was chased by the cat.» This is the passive voice. The mouse is the thing the action happens to, so it comes first. The word «by» shows who did it.
explain: To make a passive sentence, use a form of «be» (is, was, were, has been) plus a past form like chased, eaten or broken. «The cake was eaten by the dog.» You can leave out the doer too: «Mistakes were made.»
fact: Passive means something happens to the subject, rather than the subject doing the action.
fact: The passive is built from a form of «be» plus a past form, such as «was eaten» or «is made».
fact: The doer can be added with «by», or left out altogether.
fact: Scientists often use the passive: «The water was heated» says what happened, without needing to name who heated it.
fact: Passive also means letting things happen to you without acting or taking part, as in «a passive audience», and «passive smoking» means breathing in other people's smoke.
exercise: «The mouse was chased by the cat.» Which sentence means the same, in the active voice? | The mouse chased the cat | The cat was chased by the mouse | *The cat chased the mouse | The mouse ran away quickly
exercise: Which sentence is in the passive voice? | Sam kicked the ball | The children found the key | The dog ate the cake | *The key was found by the children
exercise: What does a passive audience do? | Acts out the play on stage | Sings every song loudly | Shouts and joins in with the songs | *Watches and listens without taking part
test: «The cake ___ eaten by the dog.» Which word completes the passive? | did | has run | ran | *was
test: Which word introduces the doer in a passive sentence? | the | *by | after | was
exam: Which sentence hides the doer? | I made a mistake | We made a cake | *Mistakes were made | Sam made the mistake
